screencast: no second ext-image-copy frame while one is pending

ext_register_frame_cb created a frame whenever PipeWire asked for one,
even with the previous frame not yet ready or failed.  The compositor
(Sway with wlroots' ext-image-copy-capture) then raised duplicate_frame,
"session already has a frame object", and the portal's connection ended
with a protocol error: no frame reached the stream.  Skip the request;
the pending frame is on its way.

--- a/src/screencast/ext_image_copy.c
+++ b/src/screencast/ext_image_copy.c
@@ -288,6 +288,13 @@ static int ext_register_session_cb(struct xdpw_screencast_instance *cast) {
 }
 
 static void ext_register_frame_cb(struct xdpw_screencast_instance *cast) {
+	/* A frame not yet ready or failed: the compositor refuses a second one
+	 * (duplicate_frame, "session already has a frame object"), which ends
+	 * the connection; this capture is already on its way. */
+	if (cast->ext_session.frame) {
+		logprint(TRACE, "ext: a frame is still pending");
+		return;
+	}
 	if (!cast->ext_session.capture_session) {
 		if (ext_register_session_cb(cast) != 0) {
 			logprint(ERROR, "ext: failed to register session");
